                  },
                  {
                    "src": "assets/uploads/reckon/mark-cone.svg",
                    "alt": ""
                  }
                ],
                "eyebrow": "Mark",
                "headline": "An impossible balance",
                "text": "Most of us were never taught how money works, and quietly assume everyone else was. So the bills, the balances and the what-ifs build into a low, constant hum of stress, and asking for help feels like admitting you’re behind. Reckon starts somewhere kinder: you don’t have to be good at money to keep it in balance.",
                "caption": "One colour, flat. Faces turned from the light are solid.",
                "part1Label": "Sphere",
                "part1Title": "What you’re protecting",
                "part1Text": "The nest egg: card paydown, savings, retirement. The largest form, carried on top.",
                "part2Label": "Cube",
                "part2Title": "Your unit",
                "part2Text": "The fixed monthly needs, balanced on a single corner. The more cubic, the more stable.",
                "part3Label": "Cone",
                "part3Title": "Automate the base",
                "part3Text": "Money flowing in and being directed: transfers and autopays on autopilot. A broad base whose tip carries everything."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
